# The three-tab design (design canvas "iBuilder, nouveau design", 2026-11-19): Library, Build, Settings. Library: the games of the phone as a grid or a list (toggle kept), a cover each (the icon, else the name's colour and
# initials), Play and Export IPA with a development certificate, Export IPA alone with a distribution one (get-task-allow), Set up for a game not built, Update when an update or DLC was added since the build, a tap for the
# game's sheet (its settings are a page of that same sheet, same theme), a long press for its menu, the exported apps below. Build: the build that runs, the queue (the queue page's own views), the games of this phone (Build, Rebuild, Update, Update and DLC) and the games only in
# the cloud (Download and build, Download). Settings loses the two rows that moved (Exported apps, Build queue). One accent (violet) for the primary buttons and the lit tab. An export whose game has no icon gets one drawn
# from the game's name (CoverArt). The Mods and Saves pages take the sheet's ground, accent and card colours (the Saves page too in an exported player). An exported player keeps its one screen but takes the look: the cover, a Play button in the cover's colour with the gradient, then Game settings, Saves and Logs as flat rows. The Cloud sources page is a flat list as well. Applies after 0061 (new file GameAppShelf.cs).
